/*!
    \page creator-how-to-profile-cmake-code.html
    \previouspage creator-how-tos.html

    \ingroup creator-how-to-analyze
    \ingroup creator-how-to-build-with-cmake

    \title Profile CMake code

    With the profiling support in CMake 3.18, and later, you can find out where
    CMake is spending time configuring your project.

    To profile the configuration of the startup project, select
    \uicontrol Analyze > \uicontrol {CMake Profiler}. \QC runs CMake with
    profiling for the active build configuration, and opens the trace in the
    \uicontrol Profile mode.

    \image {qtcreator-cmake-profiler.webp} {CMake profiling information in the Profile mode}

    The timeline shows the CMake commands that ran, each below the command that
    called it. The commands of the top-level \c CMakeLists.txt are in the second
    row, below \c configure. The widest bars took the most time.

    Select a command to see its arguments and the file and line that called it.
    \QC opens that file at that line next to the trace.

    The \uicontrol Statistics view lists how often each command ran and how long
    it took.

    Each run of the CMake Profiler replaces the trace of the previous run.

    \sa {CMake}, {Chrome Trace Format Visualizer}
*/
